hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17735","Muhammad ibn Bakr and Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Jurayj informed us, Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman informed me, from Ibn Masada, the companion of the army, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I have grown heavy, so whoever misses my bowing attains it in the slowness of my standing. And Abd al-Razzaq said: in the slow of my standing."
